# Timing, expectation, possession.

/* Commentary layer only. C = attributed commentator claim; R = supplied editorial bridge or comparison. All arrows are editorial. The base Gemara maps remain separate. See sources/commentary.json. */

/* C | Rashi | Rashi on Bava Metzia 21b, s.v. יאוש שלא מדעת | Base nodes: O1, O4 */
[KO1 · Rashi: the time of discovery]: C · At discovery the owner is unaware, although learning of the loss would normally bring despair. {"color": "#53659c"}
  +> <KO7 · Supplied: two distinct qualifications>

/* C | Rashi | Rashi on Bava Metzia 21b, s.v. מהשתא הוי יאוש | Base nodes: O6, O7 */
[KO2 · Rashi: explaining Rava]: C · Rava counts the response now: once the owner learns, the lost object will no longer occupy the owner’s concern. {"color": "#53659c"}
  +> <KO7 · Supplied: two distinct qualifications>

/* C | Tosafot | Tosafot on Bava Metzia 21b, s.v. דלכי נפל מיניה לא מיאש | Base nodes: O2 */
[KO3 · Tosafot: marked loss is different]: C · Later despair over a marked object is contingent; initially the owner was not standing ready to despair. {"color": "#53659c"}
  +> <KO7 · Supplied: two distinct qualifications>

/* C | Ritva (via Shittah) | Ritva (via Shittah) on Bava Metzia 21b, s.v. ורבא אמר הוי יאוש כיון דלכי ידע לא סגי דלא מייאש | Base nodes: O2, O5 */
[KO4 · Ritva (via Shittah): possession for the owner]: C · Where unnoticed despair is ineffective, pickup leaves the finder’s hand like the owner’s hand, as a custodian. {"color": "#53659c"}
  +> [KO5 · Ritva (via Shittah): later despair cannot cure it]

/* C | Ritva (via Shittah) | Ritva (via Shittah) on Bava Metzia 21b, s.v. ורבא אמר הוי יאוש כיון דלכי ידע לא סגי דלא מייאש | Base nodes: O2, O5 */
[KO5 · Ritva (via Shittah): later despair cannot cure it]: C · Because the finder did not acquire at pickup and holds for the owner, the owner’s later despair does not confer acquisition. {"color": "#53659c"}
  +> <KO7 · Supplied: two distinct qualifications>

/* C | Ritva (via Shittah) | Ritva (via Shittah) on Bava Metzia 21b, s.v. ורבא אמר הוי יאוש כיון דלכי ידע לא סגי דלא מייאש | Base nodes: O2 */
[KO6 · Ritva (via Shittah): not necessarily theft]: C · Ba-issura here describes taking while the object remains in the owner’s domain; it need not mean an intention to steal. {"color": "#53659c"}
  +> <KO7 · Supplied: two distinct qualifications>

/* R | Editorial | Rashi on Bava Metzia 21b, s.v. יאוש שלא מדעת; Rashi on Bava Metzia 21b, s.v. מהשתא הוי יאוש; Tosafot on Bava Metzia 21b, s.v. דלכי נפל מיניה לא מיאש; Ritva (via Shittah) on Bava Metzia 21b, s.v. ורבא אמר הוי יאוש כיון דלכי ידע לא סגי דלא מייאש | Base nodes: O1, O2, O5, O7 */
<KO7 · Supplied: two distinct qualifications>: R · Keep anticipated despair separate from contingent later despair, and ask whether pickup already made the finder a holder for the owner. {"color": "#f3d5a5"}

